Almost 100 African migrants hoping to travel to Algeria died of thirst after their two trucks fell in the middle of the Sahara.
Experts say the violence that caused the deaths of 14 adults and 7 children is nothing more than an unfortunate coincidence, not the sign of an escalation of violence in America.
Instead of being destabilized by shutting down government operations in the U.S., investors have remained focused on what’s probably most important: the Federal Reserve.
